              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "The domain **`rewardclub.me`** is highly likely to be a **suspicious, untrusted, or fraudulent website**. \n\nBecause this specific domain has virtually no legitimate search engine presence or official corporate backing, it is most often used as a temporary landing page for online scams. \n\n### Common Risks Associated with Domains Like This:\n\n1. **Phishing SMS and Spam Text Scams**\n   Scammers frequently send text messages or emails claiming you have \"unclaimed points,\" a \"pending package,\" or a \"gift voucher\" (often pretending to be from CVS, USPS, Amazon, or Walmart). Clicking the link takes you to a page like `rewardclub.me` to \"claim your prize\", where they will ask for a small shipping/processing fee to steal your credit card details.\n\n2. **Hidden \"Reward Club\" Subscription Traps**\n   There is a history of controversial \"Rewards Clubs\" (historically linked to companies like Easylife in the UK or Hubside in Europe) that use aggressive tactics or pre-ticked boxes to sign users up for automatic recurring fees (often around \u00a310 to \u00a370 per month or year) without their clear consent.\n\n3. **Data Harvesting**\n   These sites may exist solely to collect your personal details (name, email, phone number, address) to sell to third-party telemarketers or use for future, more targeted scams.\n\n---\n\n### What You Should Do:\n\n* **Do NOT enter any personal details or passwords.**\n* **Do NOT input your credit or debit card information.**\n* **If you have already entered your card details:** Contact your bank or credit card provider immediately. Let them know you may have entered your card on a fraudulent site. Ask them to block any unauthorized recurring charges (Continuous Payment Authorities) or replace your card.\n* **Monitor your bank statements:** Keep a close eye on your accounts over the next few months to ensure no random, small, or recurring charges appear under names like \"Reward Club,\" \"Perx,\" \"Premier Offers,\" or other unfamiliar merchants.",
